        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-43",
        "notes": "Independently checked Proof 1.1–2.1 against all nine current cited supplier statements: Cauchy–Schwarz gives coordinate and cross-product integrability; vector independence permits factoring weight products from input products; centered mutually independent weights kill off-diagonal expectations. Nonnegative factorization gives finite diagonal moments, so the finite square is integrable. Input coordinates need not be independent. n=1, zero weights and zero input moments are covered without division; n=0 is excluded. All variables are real, both random vectors are given, no AC or converse is used. Reader and refuter raise no finding. JHU Handout 8 §3 lines 108–109 corroborates the moment calculation; the local proof establishes the more general dependent-input version."
