      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-43",
        "notes": "Independently checked Proof 1.1–3.1 and all five exact supplier statements. Symmetry splits positive/negative probabilities with p0 retained; zero contributes nothing to activation moments but contributes c²p0 to the gate. L2 implies L1, so first moments and centered-variance expansion are legitimate. For every real a (including 0,1,-1) the positive/negative decomposition gives the displayed PReLU formulas. p0=1, Z=0, and p0=0 satisfy all identities; a=1,c=1 is precisely the ordinary differentiable kink case. No AC, limiting argument or unsupported converse. He et al. §2.2 and JHU §3 motivate the half moment; the atom-aware generalization is proved locally. Reader delta is sentence grammar only and preserves all formulas, hypotheses and strength; current bytes match native post and archived pre bytes match native pre."
      }
