      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-43",
        "notes": "Read every step 1.1–3.1 and all nine current supplier statements. The chain rule applies only away from all relevant ReLU zeros; signals at zeros are explicitly conventional. General finite covariance expansion needs only the stated L2 summands, also for any bounded measurable replacement gate. Conditional gate-vector/downstream independence factors h_j², while whole-matrix/h independence permits the centered-weight lemma on each column, without assuming independence among h coordinates. Iterating yields common upstream second moments and permits an uncentered terminal signal. p=1, sigma²=0 and G=0 give zero factors without illegal division. For the feasibility obstruction, symmetry and positive variance give positive strict-negative probability; finite mutual entry independence makes the all-negative-matrix event positive. Nonnegative previous ReLU outputs then force h=0 on that event, and W/h independence forces h=0 a.s.; p<1 plus gate independence forces G=0. No unstated input/weight independence is needed for that obstruction. The theorem does not misrepresent the conditional source recurrence as realizable nonzero gradients. He et al. §2.2 Eqs. (13)–(16) explicitly assume the two independences; current proof correctly treats their limitations. No AC, missing limiting argument, new defect or repair."
