      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-43",
        "notes": "Read Proof 1.1–3.1 and all seven exact current cited suppliers, including both complete recurrence proofs as prerequisite context. Rowwise centered-weight variance and symmetric PReLU moments yield the raw-input base and (1+a²)/2 hidden factor even with zero atoms and dependent coordinates. Finite substitution uses no division by V1; L=1 has the empty product value one. Backward gates are bounded for finite a,c, so gate/g independence yields E h_j²=kappa G; matrix/h independence licenses the same lemma on columns. Iteration concerns common second moments, with upstream means zero even for uncentered terminal g. p=0 gives the source scale; p=1 gives kappa=c²; a=0,c=0 matches the ReLU obstruction; a=1,c=1 gives kappa=1 at every atom probability. kappa=0 forces upstream zero and is kept separate from division. Both positive source scales agree iff positive widths agree, in both directions. Negative real slopes also satisfy the algebra and are never treated as monotone activations. No AC, limit or nonzero-gradient realizability is assumed. Checked He et al. §2.2 PReLU paragraph after Eq. (16), PDF p.5 lines 553–565, and JHU §3 lines 108–109. No defect, repair or unresolved prerequisite."
      }
