        "notes": "Independently recomputed all Verification steps 1.1–2.1 and read the three exact suppliers. First finite law has EW=0, EW²=2 and EReLU(W)²=4/3, unequal to Var(W)/2=1, with no zero atom but unequal sign probabilities. In the second independent Rademacher/uniform model WX is uniform [-2,2]; shifting by 1 gives uniform [-1,3], mean 1, variance 4/3 and positive-part second moment integral (1/4)∫0³z² dz=9/4, unequal to 2/3. Neither example purports to refute the symmetric-zero-centered supplier. Both models are nonempty with finite moments, the continuous endpoints have zero probability, and no AC or converse is involved. Source context is the symmetry and zero-bias discussion of He et al. §2.2; the exact witnesses are local calculations. No reader/refuter finding, new defect or repair."
